                        ],
                        "name": "_omnifunc",
                        "type": "setfield"
                    },
                    {
                        "documentation": " Enables or disables completions from the given language client in the given\n buffer. Effects of enabling completions are:\n\n - Calling |vim.lsp.completion.get()| uses the enabled clients to retrieve completion candidates.\n - Selecting a completion item shows a preview popup (\"completionItem/resolve\") if 'completeopt'\n   has \"popup\".\n - Accepting a completion item using `<c-y>` applies side effects like expanding snippets,\n   text edits (e.g. insert import statements) and executing associated commands. This works for\n   completions triggered via autotrigger, 'omnifunc' or [vim.lsp.completion.get()].\n\n Examples: |lsp-attach| |lsp-completion|\n\n Note: the behavior of `autotrigger=true` is controlled by the LSP `triggerCharacters` field. You\n can override it on LspAttach, see |lsp-autocompletion|.\n\n@*param* `enable` — True to enable, false to disable\n\n@*param* `client_id` — Client ID\n\n@*param* `bufnr` — Buffer handle, or 0 for the current buffer",
                        "infer": {
                            "types": [
                                {
                                    "arguments": [
                                        {
                                            "documentation": "True to enable, false to disable",
                                            "infer": {
                                                "types": [
                                                    {
                                                        "kind": "builtin",
                                                        "value": "boolean"
                                                    }
                                                ],
                                                "view": "boolean"
                                            },
                                            "name": "enable",
                                            "optional": false
                                        },
                                        {
